# Product Manager

`prd/niscorp-company-site.md` is the v1 requirements. It was written from `plan/niscorp-company-site.md`. When scope changes, edit the PRD and add a revision-log line. Do not add a roadmap or a go-to-market plan.

## In v1

A static company site as specified in the PRD: Home, a services overview, AI and websites detail pages, About, one unnamed case study, and Contact. Enterprise software is a section on the services overview. Contact is phone, email, WhatsApp, and a form that opens those apps on the visitor’s device.

The UI is part of the requirements. The pages should look modern and composed, with a clear first viewport. A pale unstyled document does not meet the PRD.

## Out until the PRD changes

Aperio by name, `/services/enterprise`, a blog, pricing, testimonials, client logos, counters, a newsletter, a backend, a form service, CSV import, and a downloaded theme.

When someone asks for one of those, say it is outside v1 and point at the PRD. A change belongs in the PRD revision log before it belongs in the build.
